# Fixed 2026-10-07, defect 409 (class improvement): a list of reports grown
# through a field copied every report before it at each push, so a file of N
# functions that run off their end cost N squared copies of a diagnostic
# before it was told: 499,500 at 1,000 functions and 7,998,000 at 4,000 on
# the base, counted per call site in an instrumented runtime. The checker
# holds them back in `c.missing_returns` and now appends them through a lent
# list (`check/state.append_diagnostic`), in place. What this case pins is
# that the list keeps every report, once, in the order the functions stand:
# 24 functions, each told at its own line. The cost is the lane's report.

function f0(x: i64) -> i64  #~ missing_return
    if x > 0
        return x

